{
  "name": "r9-recovery-restore-refuses-a-rolled-back-backup",
  "requires": "r9",
  "kind": "scenario",
  "side": "client",
  "log": "r9-vectors-membership-log",
  "note": "R9.5 (Astation r3 review 3, r4 reviews 1 and 3): a restore takes its anchor from the kit (account_id and genesis_hash, bound by kit_tag), its version floor from the log's newest k_backup entry and its freshness from host-signed accept heads (an init needs no membership). A relay serving an older log than a host signed, an older authentic backup than the newest k_backup, or an occupied but uncommitted version (the version-4 envelope while the log names version 3) is refused; a kit whose bound fields were altered, or a replaced kit, is refused before any recovery_add is published. The no-host case is r9-recovery-stale-head-withholds-the-recovery. A backup whose hash matches its k_backup entry (KB8_badct) but whose ciphertext was altered fails to open with the correct kit: backup_invalid.",
